# MathCourse HLS production template
#
# IMPORTANT:
# 1. This is an EXAMPLE only. Do not paste it into Nginx unchanged.
# 2. Replace the HLS root with the real server filesystem path.
# 3. Keep the HLS directory outside a directly browsable/public alias whenever possible.
# 4. The PHP gateway remains the fallback until this configuration is tested.
#
# Recommended final request flow:
#   WordPress / MathCourse -> permission + short-lived signature
#   Nginx -> serves m3u8 / ts directly
#
# The current PHP router signs lesson + expiry + exact media URL. If the
# production Nginx implementation is enabled, its secure-link algorithm and
# URL layout MUST match the token generator before switching traffic.

# Example protected internal location:
#
# location ^~ /math-hls-internal/ {
#     internal;
#     alias /REAL/PATH/TO/wp-content/uploads/wangke/;
#     add_header X-Content-Type-Options nosniff always;
#     add_header Cache-Control "private, no-store" always;
# }
#
# Do not add a public location for the same HLS directory. A public alias such
# as /wp-content/uploads/wangke/ would bypass the application-level protection.

# Migration checklist:
# - [ ] Confirm the real HLS filesystem path.
# - [ ] Confirm direct browser access to the original HLS URL is denied.
# - [ ] Confirm MathCourse can still obtain a short-lived playback URL.
# - [ ] Confirm m3u8 playback works on Chrome/Edge/Safari/iPhone.
# - [ ] Confirm ts/m4s segment requests are served by Nginx, not PHP-FPM.
# - [ ] Confirm an expired token is rejected.
# - [ ] Confirm an unauthorized WordPress account is rejected.
# - [ ] Confirm preview lessons still work.
# - [ ] Confirm authorized paid lessons still work.
# - [ ] Only after all checks pass, switch production traffic from PHP proxy to Nginx.
